\subsection*{1. Novelty and Contribution}

The coupling architecture between GRMHD, GW strain, RRT, and FLRW expansion is
highly original. No existing literature presents a four-way astrophysical
pipeline with cryptographic verification and encrypted metric evaluation.

\subsection*{2. Mathematical Rigor}

The derivations of:
\begin{itemize}
    \item stress-energy tensor in GRMHD,
    \item quadrupole moment extraction,
    \item Boltzmann transport in curved spacetime,
    \item FLRW backreaction,
\end{itemize}
are mathematically sound and internally consistent.

\subsection*{3. Numerical Stability}

The autonomous stability engine, including:
\begin{itemize}
    \item global residual monitoring,
    \item adaptive damping,
    \item CFL enforcement,
    \item TVD/PPM reconstruction,
\end{itemize}
is well justified and appropriate for relativistic simulations.

\subsection*{4. HPC Architecture}

The domain decomposition, MPI ghost-zone exchange, and GPU kernel design
demonstrate strong understanding of large-scale computational physics.

